# ---- heavy working material, deliberately not in the repo ----
#
# Everything below is either regenerable, over GitHub's limits, or should not be
# on a public origin. Git keeps every blob it has ever seen, so a large file
# pushed once stays in the history's weight forever and only comes out by
# rewriting it — which is why these are excluded up front rather than committed
# and tidied later.

# 323MB of extracted video frames. Regenerable with ffmpeg from the source mp4,
# which IS committed alongside them.
/Animate_image_preserve_compositi__1080p_202607251223_frames/
/Animate_image_preserve_compositi__1080p_202607251223_frames 2/

# 231MB of reference material. reference.zip is 115MB on its own, which GitHub
# rejects outright — its hard per-file ceiling is 100MB.
/reference/
/reference.zip

# 127MB of brand book, and it is sitting under public/. Anything in public/ is
# served by Next at its own path, so committing this would publish the whole
# brand book as a downloadable file at /BRAND%20BOOK.zip on the live site.
/public/BRAND BOOK/
/public/BRAND BOOK.zip
